                        "sense_id": "1fe80ced-45e0-3c3c-bb0b-d7fcab4c2be7",
                        "entry_id": "0b2319f9-71fe-35af-82af-7da479b1a7d6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A species (group of organisms that can interbreed) identified and characterised by means of genetics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2eacb56e-5bd2-4c2a-a6e9-6d9a4a0d609f",
                                "sense_id": "1fe80ced-45e0-3c3c-bb0b-d7fcab4c2be7",
                                "text": "When their respective genotypes permit inter-bacterial genetic transfer and recombination, we may say that they belong to the same genospecies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98455f8c-9e87-40da-b406-eeecd2ef71dd",
                                "sense_id": "1fe80ced-45e0-3c3c-bb0b-d7fcab4c2be7",
                                "text": "The genospecies complex of B. burgdorferi sensu lato has been divided into more than 4 distinct genospecies: B.burgdorferi sensu stricto (most North American isolates), Borrella garinii, Borrelia afzelii, Borrelia japonica, and other additional strains which do not fit into any of the specified genospecies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5196162-171e-4845-b9fd-8263cdaa9918",
                                "sense_id": "1fe80ced-45e0-3c3c-bb0b-d7fcab4c2be7",
                                "text": "The last two genospecies are etiologic agents of almost all LB cases in Russia, which encompasses the greater part of the range of B."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
